%% section: Replication modes
%% caption: Synchronous versus asynchronous
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant P as Primary
    participant R as Replica
    C->>P: write
    P->>P: append to WAL
    alt asynchronous
        P-->>C: committed
        P->>R: ship WAL later
        Note over P,R: fast, but a primary loss costs everything not yet shipped
    else synchronous
        P->>R: ship WAL
        R-->>P: acknowledged
        P-->>C: committed
        Note over P,R: no data loss on failover, and every commit pays the round trip
    end
